@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
    ViewData["Description"] = "Review Immaculate Heart Hospital Kereita's patient privacy policy and data protection practices for medical records, billing, and clinical confidentiality.";
    ViewData["Keywords"] = "hospital privacy policy, patient data protection, Kenya medical privacy";
    ViewData["OgImage"] = "https://immaculatehearthospitalkereita.org/images/logo.jpg";
}

<section class="bg-primary text-white text-center py-5" style="background: linear-gradient(rgba(0, 74, 153, 0.9), rgba(0, 40, 90, 0.95));">
    <div class="container py-5">
        <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold mb-3">Patient Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="lead fw-bold" style="font-size: 1.3rem; text-shadow: 0 2px 4px rgba(0,0,0,0.3);">How we protect, manage, and safeguard your medical and personal data.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<div class="container my-5">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
        <div class="col-lg-10">
            <div class="card shadow-sm p-4 p-md-5 border-0 bg-white rounded-3">
                
                <p class="lead text-secondary mb-4">
                    <strong>Immaculate Heart Hospital Kereita</strong> ("we," "our," or "the Hospital") is committed to protecting the privacy and confidentiality of our patients' personal health information. This Privacy Policy outlines how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard your information in compliance with the <strong>Kenya Data Protection Act, 2019</strong> and medical ethics regulations.
                </p>

                <hr class="my-4">

                <div class="mb-4">
                    <h3 class="h4 text-primary fw-bold mb-3">1. Information We Collect</h3>
                    <p class="text-muted">To provide you with quality healthcare services, we collect both personal and sensitive medical data, including:</p>
                    <ul class="text-muted ps-4">
                        <li><strong>Personal Identification:</strong> Full name, national identity card number/passport number, date of birth, gender, and physical address.</li>
                        <li><strong>Contact Information:</strong> Phone number and email address.</li>
                        <li><strong>Medical & Health Records:</strong> Clinical history, diagnoses, symptoms, laboratory test results, pharmaceutical prescriptions, radiological images (ultrasound, X-ray), and treatment plans.</li>
                        <li><strong>Financial & Insurance Data:</strong> Details related to your Social Health Authority (SHA) coverage, private corporate insurance (e.g., Britam), or out-of-pocket billing records.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <div class="mb-4">
                    <h3 class="h4 text-primary fw-bold mb-3">2. How We Use Your Information</h3>
                    <p class="text-muted">Your data is processed strictly for legitimate healthcare and administrative workflows, which include:</p>
                    <ul class="text-muted ps-4">
                        <li>Delivering accurate medical diagnosis, inpatient/outpatient treatment, and continuous nursing care.</li>
                        <li>Managing hospital admission records, specialist clinic appointments, and emergency triaging.</li>
                        <li>Processing payment claims with medical insurance companies, SHA, or other legal financial sponsors.</li>
                        <li>Complying with statutory public health reporting mandates issued by the Ministry of Health (MoH), Kenya.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <div class="mb-4">
                    <h3 class="h4 text-primary fw-bold mb-3">3. Disclosure and Data Sharing</h3>
                    <p class="text-muted">We maintain strict medical confidentiality. We do not sell, rent, or trade your data. Information sharing only occurs under the following controlled circumstances:</p>
                    <ul class="text-muted ps-4">
                        <li><strong>Medical Referrals:</strong> Sharing critical data with external specialists or laboratory labs when you are explicitly referred for higher-level diagnostic evaluation.</li>
                        <li><strong>Insurance Verification:</strong> Sending treatment details to SHA or private underwriters to authorize payment coverage for procedures.</li>
                        <li><strong>Legal Mandates:</strong> Disclosing specific infectious disease tracking parameters or court-ordered records to authorized government entities as prescribed by Kenyan law.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <div class="mb-4">
                    <h3 class="h4 text-primary fw-bold mb-3">4. Security of Medical Records</h3>
                    <p class="text-muted">
                        We implement advanced organizational and technical security measures to protect your physical and Electronic Health Records (EHR) against unauthorized access, loss, or alteration. Access to your clinical database file is restricted strictly to authorized medical personnel actively involved in your therapeutic care loop.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="mb-4">
                    <h3 class="h4 text-primary fw-bold mb-3">5. Your Patient Rights</h3>
                    <p class="text-muted">Under the Kenya Data Protection Act, you possess clear rights regarding your personal records, including:</p>
                    <ul class="text-muted ps-4">
                        <li>The right to request access to your official medical record files and histories.</li>
                        <li>The right to demand corrections or updates to inaccurate biographical or historical personal data.</li>
                        <li>The right to object to or restrict specific processing paths of your data (subject to overarching clinical safety requirements).</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <div class="mb-4">
                    <h3 class="h4 text-primary fw-bold mb-3">6. Policy Updates</h3>
                    <p class="text-muted">
                        We reserve the right to modify this operational privacy declaration occasionally to capture localized regulatory movements or administrative expansions. Any revisions take effect immediately upon being posted publicly to our online frameworks.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="alert alert-light border border-2 mt-5 p-4 rounded-3">
                    <h5 class="fw-bold text-dark mb-2">Privacy Questions & Inquiries</h5>
                    <p class="text-muted small mb-0">
                        If you have queries regarding our data security practices or wish to file a formal request concerning your data access rights, please contact our hospital data administrative officer directly at <strong>info@@immaculatehearthospitalkereita.org</strong> or visit the main information desk at our facility in Kereita.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <p class="text-muted text-center mt-4 mb-0 small">
                    <em>Document Reference: IHHK-PP-2026-V1 &bull; Last Updated: May 2026</em>
                </p>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>